Section 3 - Scope
(2)
This Policy applies to scholarships for current or future domestic coursework students that are funded:
wholly by the University;
by government, industry, philanthropic or other external organisations, wholly, or in part with the University.
(3)
This Policy does not apply to:
graduate research scholarships (these are covered by the
Graduate Research and RTP Scholarships Policy
);
fee waivers applied to domestic or international students (see
Student Fees Policy
);
prizes.
(4)
The parameters and funding arrangements for external scholarships are included in this Policy. As the University has no administrative oversight of such scholarships the management of and selection for external scholarships is outside the scope of this Policy (see individual scholarships for further information).

Internal Scholarships
(11)
Internal scholarships (as distinct from external scholarships) are defined by all of the following parameters:
funding is from the University, or an external donor;
La Trobe University normally sets the eligibility criteria and terms and conditions of the scholarship with the following variations:
in the case of philanthropically-funded scholarships,this is done in partnership with the donor, aligning to the mission, values and strategic direction of La Trobe;
in the case of Government-funded Indigenous scholarships, eligibility criteria and terms and conditions are set by the Federal Government.
students apply through the Victorian Tertiary Admissions Centre (VTAC) process or the University provides the scholarship application form directly to the applicant and is responsible for the selection and management of the scholarship;
applications are open to all current and future La Trobe University students that meet the eligibility criteria.

External Scholarships
(12)
Any person, group or organisation within or external to the University may propose the establishment of a scholarship.
(13)
An external scholarship is defined by all of the following parameters:
the organisation offering the scholarship sets the eligibility criteria, terms and conditions, selection and management parameters independently of La Trobe University.
the scholarship is assessed by the Advancement Office as being aligned with the University’s values and strategic direction;
La Trobe University may communicate the availability of an external scholarship on its scholarships’ web page and by other means if the scholarship:
is provided by a reputable and recognised organisation or institution where the scholarship is clearly for the purposes of goodwill rather than marketing or recruitment;
aligns with the values of La Trobe University;
represents significant value and more than a one-off payment;
is deemed to have longevity in its existence;
if subject specific, then for a subject or discipline that aligns with the offerings of the University;
is not a prize, awarded as a result of submitting a piece of work;
is offered by an Australian charitable organisation.
(14)
La Trobe University takes no responsibility for the selection or management of external scholarships and makes this clear to students.

Part D -  Scholarship Conditions
(25)
The University offers a range of scholarships, available for both full-time and part-time study.
(26)
Where a scholarship is exempt from income tax, the conditions must be consistent with Australian taxation requirements for income tax exemption for the recipient. This means that:
scholarships are for educational purposes only;
there is no requirement for the recipient to become, or remain, an employee of the scholarship provider at the time of receipt of the scholarship or in the future;
the scholarship is open to a range of recipients;
the recipient is normally enrolled full-time in the relevant course of study, except as provided for under taxation legislation, and;
the scholarship is paid by the University.
(27)
The University does not provide advice to scholarship recipients about any personal financial or taxation implications but may inform them that scholarships may affect income tax liability or Centrelink payments.

Section 7 - Definitions
(58)
For the purposes of this Policy:
access or equity award: a scholarship awarded based on La Trobe’s standard equity rubric rating;
merit-based or excellence award: a scholarship awarded based on academic performance;
prize: a one-off award in recognition of past outstanding achievement that does not require an application;
scholarship: a multi-year award offered on a competitive basis, which may require an application, to prospective or current students that supports them in their studies.
